Below is the analysis of the issue and a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch that restores the missing `bx--table-column-checkbox` class on each selectable‐row cell.

1) Bug scenario & root cause  
   - On the vanilla example in the CSS/HTML playground, each checkbox‐cell is wrapped in  
     `<td class="bx--table-column-checkbox">…</td>`, which enforces the 48px row height.  
   - In the React DataTable, `TableSelectRow` simply renders `<td className={className}>…</td>`, but `getSelectionProps` never supplies a default `className` (and the consumer doesn’t pass one), so you end up with `<td>…</td>` and lose the Carbon styles.  

2) Fix  
   - In `TableSelectRow.js`, prepend the required `bx--table-column-checkbox` CSS class on the wrapping `<td>`.  
   - If a user ever passes their own `className`, it will be appended.

